# This tree is checked out, copied and edited on Windows, where core.autocrlf is false. Without a
# rule here, a copy that arrives with CRLF ends up looking like a modification of every text file it
# touches (measured: 5359 of 5387) and a reviewable diff is impossible; the shell scripts would stop
# running, since their interpreter reads a carriage return as part of a name. LF in the repository
# and LF in the checkout is what the tree already holds, so stating it costs nothing and keeps it so.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes that must survive untouched: fixtures, images, compiled blobs.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.bin binary
*.dat binary
*.hc binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
